Step 1 is done and pushed (`e122a6b`, `6fffc40`). `docs/idiomatic-mlpl.md` covers:
- the idioms from 18 companion repos, each with a real snippet and path;
- the `@formula`/`@ascii`/`@source`/`@note` math-annotation convention and demo-ml-utils' notation rules;
- an anti-pattern and workaround table;
- how the three microgpt variants will use each idiom.

The new saga, `literate-variants`, is set up with 6 steps, and the finished one is archived.

Step 2, `docs/sw-mlpl-requests.md`, is next. It waits on the third survey (downstream workarounds, and what sw-mlpl already tracks or has rejected), which is still running. I'll continue when it reports back.

